AB  - We tested whether NF-κB pathway is indispensable for the increase in expression of E3-ligases and unloading-induced muscle atrophy using IKKβ inhibitor IMD-0354.  Three groups of rats were used: nontreated control (C), 3 days of  unloading/hindlimb suspension with (HS+IMD) or without (HS) IMD-0354. Levels of  IκBα were higher in HS+IMD (1.16-fold) and lower in HS (0.82-fold) when compared  with C group. IMD-0354 treatment during unloading: had no effect on loss of  muscle mass; increased mRNA levels of MuRF1 and MAFbx; increased levels of  pFoxO3; and had no effect on levels of Bcl-3, p105, and p50 proteins. Our study  for the first time showed that inhibiting IKKβ in vivo during 3-day unloading  failed to diminish expression of ubiquitin ligases and prevent muscle atrophy.
